IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore): s 7A -- the solvency statement, its content and form, how the directors form their
-- opinion, and the offence of making one without reasonable grounds.
--
-- The thing the directors make is the core's `Solvency statement`: what it says and how it was made out, as a witness could
-- read it off the document. The rules here decide whether it is a solvency statement (s 7A(1)), whether it is in the form
-- s 7A(2) asks, and what follows for a director who makes one with no reasonable grounds (s 7A(6)).
-- Whether the company is exempt from audit under s 205B or 205C is a fact asked here as an input (a later part encodes those
-- sections); so is whether the financial statements the directors looked at comply with s 201(2) and (5).

§ `Section 7A(1): the content`

-- (1)(b): the opinion matched to the intention. Where winding up is intended within 12 months, the opinion is that the company can
-- pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up (limb (i)); where it is not, that it can pay its
-- debts as they fall due during the 12 months after the statement (limb (ii)).
-- src:2289 | 7A.—(1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,
-- src:2290 | “solvency statement”, in relation to a proposed redemption of
-- src:2291 | preference shares by a company out of its capital under section 70,
-- src:2296 | a proposed giving of financial assistance by a company under
-- src:2297 | section 76(9A) or (9B) or a proposed reduction by a company of its
-- src:2298 | share capital under section 78B or 78C, means a statement by the
-- src:2299 | directors of the company that they have formed the opinion —
-- src:2301 | (a) that, as regards the company’s situation at the date of the
-- src:2302 | statement, there is no ground on which the company could
-- src:2303 | then be found to be unable to pay its debts;
-- src:2305 | (b) where —
-- src:2307 | (i) it is intended to commence winding up of the
-- src:2308 | company within the period of 12 months
-- src:2309 | immediately after the date of the statement, that
-- src:2310 | the company will be able to pay its debts in full
-- src:2311 | within the period of 12 months after the date of
-- src:2312 | commencement of the winding up; or
-- src:2314 | (ii) it is not intended so to commence winding up, that
-- src:2315 | the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall
-- src:2316 | due during the period of 12 months immediately after
-- src:2317 | the date of the statement; and
-- src:2319 | (c) that the value of the company’s assets is not less than the
-- src:2320 | value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities) and
-- src:2321 | will not, after the proposed redemption, giving of financial
-- src:2322 | assistance or reduction (as the case may be), become less
-- src:2323 | than the value of its liabilities (including contingent
-- src:2324 | liabilities),
-- src:2326 | being a statement which complies with subsection (2). [36/2014]
@ref s 7A(1) (src:2289-2326)
GIVEN statement IS A `Solvency statement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7A(1)(b) the statement gives the opinion that the intention calls for` MEANS
    IF statement's `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months immediately after its date`
    THEN statement's `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up`
    ELSE statement's `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months immediately after its date`

-- (1): "solvency statement", in relation to the three proposals, means a statement by the directors that they have formed the opinion
-- (a), (b) and (c) ... being a statement which complies with subsection (2). This function is the content, (a) to (c); the form is s 7A(2).
@ref s 7A(1) (src:2289-2326)
GIVEN statement IS A `Solvency statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` MEANS
    IF statement's `the proposal it concerns` EQUALS `some other proposal`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "solvency statement, in relation to a proposed redemption ..., a proposed giving of financial assistance ... or a proposed reduction ..., means" -- the definition names three proposals and no other
    ELSE (IF     statement's `it is a statement by the directors of the company`
             AND statement's `it says the directors have formed the opinion that, as regards the company's situation at its date, there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts`
             AND `s 7A(1)(b) the statement gives the opinion that the intention calls for` statement
             AND statement's `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`
             AND statement's `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a statement by the directors that they have formed the opinion (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 7A(2): the form`

-- (2)(a): a company exempt from audit under s 205B or 205C: a written declaration signed by every director.
-- (2)(b): any other company: a written declaration signed by every director, or accompanied by the auditor's report.
-- src:2327 | (2) The solvency statement —
-- src:2329 | (a) if the company is exempt from audit requirements under
-- src:2330 | section 205B or 205C, must be in the form of a written
-- src:2331 | declaration signed by every director; or
-- src:2333 | (b) if the company is not such a company, must be in the form
-- src:2334 | of a written declaration signed by every director or must be
-- src:2335 | accompanied by a report from its auditor that the auditor
-- src:2336 | has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the
-- src:2341 | opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the
-- src:2342 | circumstances.
@ref s 7A(2) (src:2327-2342)
GIVEN statement IS A `Solvency statement`
      `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`
    THEN (IF statement's `the number of directors who have signed it as a written declaration` EQUALS statement's `the number of directors of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C, must be in the form of a written declaration signed by every director" (a duty not met, the provision's own question)
    ELSE (IF    statement's `the number of directors who have signed it as a written declaration` EQUALS statement's `the number of directors of the company`
             OR statement's `it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the company is not such a company, must be in the form of a written declaration signed by every director or must be accompanied by a report from its auditor" (a duty not met, the provision's own question)

-- (1) as a whole: the content and the form.
-- src:2326 | being a statement which complies with subsection (2). [36/2014]
@ref s 7A(1) (src:2326-2326)
GIVEN statement IS A `Solvency statement`
      `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` MEANS
    IF `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` statement EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the definition names three proposals and no other
    ELSE (IF     (`s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` statement EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             AND (`s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` statement `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a statement ... being a statement which complies with subsection (2)" (a "means" definition)

§ `Sections 7A(3) to (5): how the directors form their opinion`

-- src:2346 | (3) In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and
-- src:2347 | (b), the directors of the company must take into account all liabilities
-- src:2348 | of the company (including contingent liabilities).
@ref s 7A(3) (src:2346-2348)
GIVEN `the directors took into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(3) the directors have formed the opinion as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the directors took into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the company must take into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)" (a duty not met, the provision's own question)

-- src:2350 | (4) In determining, for the purposes of subsection (1)(c), whether
-- src:2351 | the value of the company’s assets is or will become less than the value
-- src:2352 | of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities) the directors of the
-- src:2353 | company —
-- src:2355 | (a) must have regard to —
-- src:2357 | (i) the most recent financial statements of the company
-- src:2358 | that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case
-- src:2359 | may be; and
-- src:2361 | (ii) all other circumstances that the directors know or
-- src:2362 | ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the
-- src:2363 | company’s assets and the value of its liabilities
-- src:2364 | (including contingent liabilities); and
-- src:2366 | (b) may rely on valuations of assets or estimates of liabilities
-- src:2367 | that are reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 7A(4) (src:2350-2367)
GIVEN `the directors had regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors had regard to all other circumstances that they know or ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the company's assets and the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(4)(a) the directors have had regard to what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the directors had regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be`
      AND `the directors had regard to all other circumstances that they know or ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the company's assets and the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the company (a) must have regard to (i) ...; and (ii) ..." (a duty not met, the provision's own question)

-- (4)(b): the directors "may rely on valuations of assets or estimates of liabilities that are reasonable in the circumstances".
@ref s 7A(4)(b) (src:2350-2367)
GIVEN `the valuation or estimate is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(4)(b) the directors may rely on the valuation or estimate` MEANS
    IF `the valuation or estimate is reasonable in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may rely on valuations ... that are reasonable in the circumstances") whose limit is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-S3 in NOTES.md)

-- (5): the directors "may take into account (a) the likelihood of the contingency occurring; and (b) any claim the company is entitled
-- to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability".
-- src:2371 | (5) In determining, for the purposes of subsection (4), the value of a
-- src:2372 | contingent liability, the directors of a company may take into
-- src:2373 | account —
-- src:2375 | (a) the likelihood of the contingency occurring; and
-- src:2377 | (b) any claim the company is entitled to make and can
-- src:2378 | reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the
-- src:2379 | contingent liability.
@ref s 7A(5) (src:2371-2379)
GIVEN `the matter is the likelihood of the contingency occurring` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a claim the company is entitled to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(5) the directors may take the matter into account in valuing a contingent liability` MEANS
    IF    `the matter is the likelihood of the contingency occurring`
       OR `the matter is a claim the company is entitled to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may take into account (a) ...; and (b) ..." lists two matters without "only", and says nothing of any other

§ `Section 7A(6): the offence`

DECLARE `s 7A(6) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A director of a company who makes a solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it.
-- Whether the company later fails is not an element (the text asks whether there were reasonable grounds when it was made).
-- src:2381 | (6) A director of a company who makes a solvency statement
-- src:2382 | without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it
-- src:2383 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:2384 | not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:2385 | 3 years or to both.
@ref s 7A(6) (src:2381-2385)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(6) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director of the company`
      AND `the person made the solvency statement`
      AND (NOT `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i) of the keel brief, fork line F-S1 in NOTES.md): "A director of a company who makes a solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence

@ref s 7A(6) (src:2381-2385)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 7A(6) penalty`
`s 7A(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 7A(6) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is a director of the company` `the person made the solvency statement` `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 7A(6) penalty` OF 100000, 3, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Regulative rules: the duties and the prohibition of s 7A(3), (4)(a) and (6)`

DECLARE `s 7A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 7A(3) take into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)`
    `s 7A(4)(a)(i) have regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5)`
    `s 7A(4)(a)(ii) have regard to all other circumstances that the directors know or ought to know affect the value of the company's assets and liabilities`
    `s 7A(6) make a solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it`

-- s 7A(3): "the directors of the company must take into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)".
-- A MUST with no time limit and no consequence the text states: no trace can show it breached (a late act still reads FULFILLED).
-- src:2346 | (3) In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and
-- src:2347 | (b), the directors of the company must take into account all liabilities
-- src:2348 | of the company (including contingent liabilities).
@ref s 7A(3) (src:2346-2348)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 7A act`
`s 7A(3) a director must take into account all liabilities` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 7A(3) take into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 7A(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not take into account all liabilities of the company, including contingent liabilities" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 7A(4)(a)(i) and (ii): the directors must have regard to the financial statements, and to all other circumstances. Same: no time limit, no breach path.
-- src:2350 | (4) In determining, for the purposes of subsection (1)(c), whether
-- src:2351 | the value of the company’s assets is or will become less than the value
-- src:2352 | of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities) the directors of the
-- src:2353 | company —
-- src:2355 | (a) must have regard to —
-- src:2357 | (i) the most recent financial statements of the company
-- src:2358 | that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case
-- src:2359 | may be; and
-- src:2361 | (ii) all other circumstances that the directors know or
-- src:2362 | ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the
-- src:2363 | company’s assets and the value of its liabilities
-- src:2364 | (including contingent liabilities); and
@ref s 7A(4)(a) (src:2350-2364)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 7A act`
`s 7A(4)(a) a director must have regard to the financial statements` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 7A(4)(a)(i) have regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5)`
    HENCE (PARTY Director `the name of the director`
           MUST `s 7A(4)(a)(ii) have regard to all other circumstances that the directors know or ought to know affect the value of the company's assets and liabilities`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
           -- no LEST: s 7A(4)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not have regard to all other circumstances that the directors know or ought to know" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    -- no LEST: s 7A(4)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not have regard to the most recent financial statements of the company" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 7A(6): the prohibition derived from the offence (the N2 ruling of 2026-11-04: where the text names the bearer, SHANT is derived).
-- A director who makes the statement without reasonable grounds breaches it; there is no time limit, so a director who never makes one has not breached it.
-- src:2381 | (6) A director of a company who makes a solvency statement
-- src:2382 | without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it
-- src:2383 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:2384 | not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:2385 | 3 years or to both.
@ref s 7A(6) (src:2381-2385)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 7A act`
`s 7A(6) a director must not make a solvency statement without reasonable grounds` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    SHANT `s 7A(6) make a solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director made a solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it"
